1
00:05:57,272 --> 00:06:03,272
The music and the magic come together...

2
00:11:54,545 --> 00:12:00,545
'Round Midnight is a drama, music film directed by Bertrand Tavernier.

3
00:17:51,818 --> 00:17:57,818
Inside the Blue Note nightclub one night in 1959 Paris, an aged,
ailing jazzman coaxes an eloquent wail from his tenor sax.

4
00:23:49,090 --> 00:23:55,090
Outside, a young Parisian too broke to buy a glass
of wine strains to hear those notes.

5
00:29:46,363 --> 00:29:52,363
Soon they will form a friendship that sparks a final burst of genius.

6
00:35:43,636 --> 00:35:49,636
Dale Turner, played by Dexter Gordon.

7
00:41:40,909 --> 00:41:46,909
Francis Borler, played by François Cluzet.

8
00:47:38,181 --> 00:47:44,181
Bérangère, played by Gabrielle Haker.

9
00:53:35,454 --> 00:53:41,454
Sylvie, played by Christine Pascal.

10
00:59:32,727 --> 00:59:38,727
le père de Francis, played by Pierre Trabaud.

11
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
la mère de Francis, played by Frédérique Meininger.

12
01:11:27,272 --> 01:11:33,272
Round Midnight is a 1986 American musical drama film directed by
Bertrand Tavernier and written by Tavernier and David Rayfiel.

13
01:17:24,545 --> 01:17:30,545
It stars Dexter Gordon, with a soundtrack by Herbie Hancock.

14
01:23:21,818 --> 01:23:27,818
The title comes from Thelonious Monk's 1943 composition "'Round Midnight",
which is featured in this film in a Hancock arrangement.

15
01:29:19,090 --> 01:29:25,090
The protagonist jazzman, Dale Turner, is based on a composite of real-life
jazz legends Lester Young (tenor sax) and Bud Powell (piano).

16
01:35:16,363 --> 01:35:22,363
While the film is fictionalized, it is drawn directly from the memoir/biography Dance of the Infidels written by French author
Francis Paudras, who had befriended Powell during his Paris expatriate days and on whom the character Francis was based.

17
01:41:13,636 --> 01:41:19,636
Gordon was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor and won a Grammy for the film's soundtrack entitled
The Other Side of Round Midnight in the category for Best Instrumental Jazz Performance, Soloist.

18
01:47:10,909 --> 01:47:16,909
Hancock won the Academy Award for Best Original Score.

19
01:53:08,181 --> 01:53:14,181
The soundtrack was released in two parts: Round Midnight
and The Other Side of Round Midnight.

20
01:59:05,454 --> 01:59:11,454
The film explores themes of jazz, musician, jazz singer
or musician, saxophonist, saxophone.

21
02:05:02,727 --> 02:05:08,727
The tone is emotional.
